00:30:08.720 --> 00:30:12.640
<v Mike>I don't know what they refer to that person who tells you when the turns are coming up.

00:30:12.760 --> 00:30:16.420
<v Mike>But like they're shouting that stuff in your ears and you have to anticipate it.

00:30:16.520 --> 00:30:18.900
<v Mike>And you're driving in the car and there's mud everywhere.

00:30:18.900 --> 00:30:21.820
<v Mike>And I was like, this is incredibly impressive.

00:30:21.820 --> 00:30:23.380
<v Mike>I can't do any of it.

00:30:23.580 --> 00:30:25.500
<v Mike>I can't drive this car.

00:30:25.960 --> 00:30:28.820
<v Mike>And it like pretty much turned me off rally games in general.

00:30:28.820 --> 00:30:32.340
<v Mike>I've tried a few other ones for two to three minutes.

00:30:32.340 --> 00:30:35.560
<v Mike>And I realize it's every time I can't drive these cars.

00:30:36.340 --> 00:30:43.760
<v Sean>Now, has that caused you to not be interested in rally as a sport in general or?

00:30:44.040 --> 00:30:46.700
<v Mike>No, I want to watch rally stuff in real life.

00:30:47.040 --> 00:30:48.080
<v Mike>Yeah, just the games.

00:30:48.160 --> 00:30:51.680
<v Mike>I just know now that I'm not good at them and it's not worth pursuing.

00:30:51.680 --> 00:30:56.840
<v Mike>But I would want to watch rally for the same reason I want to watch the free solo guy climb buildings.

00:30:56.840 --> 00:30:59.380
<v Mike>You know, I'm hoping to see something really cool happen.

00:31:00.520 --> 00:31:01.820
<v Joe>Something really cool.

00:31:02.020 --> 00:31:04.820
<v Mike>Cool, huh? Yeah, something really cool happened.

00:31:06.460 --> 00:31:08.200
<v Mike>Something you don't see every day.

00:31:11.820 --> 00:31:22.920
<v Mike>And I mean, there's also the, as you could tell from my attitude towards them, the realization that I have no idea how to coach a hockey team.

00:31:23.540 --> 00:31:28.060
<v Mike>That like, you know, the NHL games kind of exposed me to being like a phony.

00:31:28.680 --> 00:31:30.820
<v Mike>Whereas like baseball, I feel like I have an idea.

00:31:31.580 --> 00:31:39.840
<v Mike>You know, like when I play baseball games, I feel like I'm in control and I can manage the team and I can make the plays and I can call the plays.

00:31:39.840 --> 00:31:46.540
<v Mike>Because the NHL was, the NHL games were like an eye opener where I was like, I guess I really don't know anything other besides offsides and icing.

00:31:47.520 --> 00:31:49.520
<v Mike>I'm not even talking about from like a rules perspective.

00:31:49.520 --> 00:31:51.820
<v Mike>I'm just talking about like a strategy perspective.

00:31:52.160 --> 00:31:58.640
<v Mike>Like, I guess I really don't understand like skating formations and line changes and shit like that.

00:31:58.800 --> 00:32:01.200
<v Mike>Like, it just happens and we're lucky to see it.

00:32:01.200 --> 00:32:14.640
<v Sean>My problem with NHL was always just that like the, the, the, when you change the difficulty, like pro was just like, you can just score anytime you put the puck towards the net.

00:32:14.680 --> 00:32:21.960
<v Sean>And then all star or whatever the equivalent is, every goalie, like would just read your inputs.

00:32:21.960 --> 00:32:30.200
<v Sean>So I could never find that middle ground where like I'd get realistic scores because it's not fun to win seven to nothing or seven to two or whatever.

00:32:30.200 --> 00:32:45.320
<v Mike>So I think you've touched into something there, Sean, because that is how I feel about a lot of sports games in that N64 PS1 era as well, where once you figure these games out, it's very easy to just win ridiculous games.

00:32:45.480 --> 00:32:48.200
<v Mike>Like your baseball games can be like 19 nothing.

00:32:48.440 --> 00:32:52.800
<v Mike>And it's like, you know, that has happened, but it doesn't happen every single time you play.

00:32:53.200 --> 00:32:57.760
<v Mike>And yet that's what I was saying at the beginning is like, that's some of the stuff that like the formative games.

00:32:57.760 --> 00:33:02.740
<v Mike>Like when I think about Wayne Gretzky's 3D hockey or MLB featuring Ken Griffey Jr.

00:33:03.040 --> 00:33:07.260
<v Mike>Like those are two N64 games that I loved playing as a kid.

00:33:07.360 --> 00:33:15.580
<v Mike>And I, you know, I had kid like motor reflexes, so I wasn't winning crazy games or anything, but I was having so much fun.

00:33:15.780 --> 00:33:21.100
<v Mike>But on revisit, like those games aren't even close to the greatest sports games of all time.

00:33:21.100 --> 00:33:22.400
<v Mike>They were just like for me.

00:33:22.560 --> 00:33:28.520
<v Mike>And now I remember the sounds and the music and the rosters more than anything else.

00:33:28.520 --> 00:33:42.160
<v Sean>Yeah, I feel especially in that area, like with PlayStation 1, at least for me, you just you can't take your eyes off of the how like choppy it is.

00:33:42.280 --> 00:33:48.200
<v Sean>And it just doesn't feel this doesn't feel right anymore because you're trained on more modern games.

00:33:48.200 --> 00:34:01.040
<v Sean>And I think like, you know, with with a video game, like with an action game or like an adventure game that that might not be as as big of a deal because like the game is the game.

00:34:01.240 --> 00:34:02.840
<v Sean>Like Mario was Mario.

00:34:07.100 --> 00:34:12.760
<v Sean>But then sports games like you're basically playing the same thing year after year for decades.

00:34:13.380 --> 00:34:24.440
<v Sean>And I think it's just a lot performance and stuff like that become a big, much bigger deal when it's the same basic gameplay that hasn't really changed over decades.

00:34:25.480 --> 00:34:38.080
<v Mike>So to wrap up the episode, I think we just have to quickly mention that Super Spike V-Ball and the World Cup being offered together doesn't make it an essential game.

00:34:38.340 --> 00:34:41.480
<v Mike>Can we agree to that? Yes, absolutely.

00:34:42.240 --> 00:34:43.500
<v Mike>You know, I think it's funny, though.

00:34:43.620 --> 00:34:53.860
<v Mike>It's like if they release a combo pack of the Legend of Zelda and the Legend of Zelda 2 Adventures of Link, is it like, oh, well, now it's on the essential games last conversation.

00:34:54.200 --> 00:34:57.080
<v Joe>I mean, it's funny because like, I just don't know.

00:34:57.240 --> 00:35:01.820
<v Joe>Even if it's like Super Mario Brothers 3 and the Legend of Zelda combo pack, I'm like, I don't know.

00:35:01.900 --> 00:35:02.860
<v Joe>That's not a game.

00:35:03.740 --> 00:35:06.700
<v Joe>Right. I still might not be like, yeah, this is an essential game.

00:35:06.860 --> 00:35:07.960
<v Mike>I would say that cartridge.

00:35:08.280 --> 00:35:09.700
